Ze-Reviewed-Against: go.fd.io/govpp v0.13.0

Upstream pull request: none opened yet.

The PPPoE ownership requirement in
plan/post-release/features/spec-pppoe-vpp-dataplane.md, AC-16, requires the
session socket to be "closed exactly once by its one owner".
Completing that lifetime also requires its native API cleanup writer and
reader to join. The upstream Unix adapter can block indefinitely in a buffered
Flush, or wait behind that writer while disconnecting. A Go context cannot
interrupt that syscall.

Bound native writes and publish the shutdown deadline before joining readers
or waiting for a writer. A separate deadline mutex serializes publication,
selection and reset, so an ordinary writer cannot overwrite or clear the
shutdown bound. Refuse queued ordinary sends after shutdown starts, preserve
the graceful client-delete request, and close a partially written connection
before another message can use it. Ignore an already closed native socket at
the final close, since a failed partial write already poisoned it.

Design: docs/contributing/patching-the-standard-library.md, "Patching a
vendored module". Apply and commit the patched vendor file through the
canonical vendor publication route. Delete this patch when Ze requires an
upstream release containing the repair.

